"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1016/j.msec.2020.111106","year":2020,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-000646","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"To determine the octanol–water distribution coefficient (log D), the shake-flask method was used. UV–visible calibration curves of the complexes were performed in n-octanol using 5% DMSO. To carry out the measurements, the complexes were solubilized in a mixture containing equal volumes of n-octanol and water containing 5% DMSO, and were kept under stirring for 18 h at 298 K. The concentration of complexes in the organic phase was determined spectrophotometrically, and the log D values were calculated through the equation: log D = log(([complex]n-octanol)/([complex]water))"}]}